<header><p class="st-kicker">margraviate · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">March of Ivrea</h1><p class="st-meta">888 CE – 1015 CE (approx.) · capital Ivrea</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">March in north-western Italy whose Anscarid rulers, Berengar II and Arduin, both seized the Italian crown.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 888–891 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-iii-of-spoleto">Guy of Spoleto</a>, contending for the Italian crown, created a march around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Ivrea</a> for his Burgundian ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anscar-i-of-ivrea">Anscar</a>, guarding the Alpine passes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aosta-valley">Aosta valley</a> and the western Po plain. Anscar's descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anscarids">Anscarids</a>, held it for more than a century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Ivrea</a> controlled a large area of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anscar-i-of-ivrea">Anscar</a>'s grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-ii-of-italy">Berengar II</a>, after exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, made himself King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 950 with his son Adalbert, until Otto I forced him to submit in 952 and deposed him in 961. A later margrave, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arduin-of-ivrea">Arduin</a>, was elected king in 1002 in opposition to the German emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Henry II</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Henry II</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arduin-of-ivrea">Arduin</a>, who retired to the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fruttuaria-abbey">Fruttuaria</a> and died in 1015. The march was then broken up, its lands divided among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and other families, notably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arduinici">Arduinici of Turin</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="margraviate, 888 CE – 1015 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">margraviate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:77.37%;width:2.53%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>888 CE – 1015 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>margraviate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ivrea</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anscar I, Berengar II, Arduin of Ivrea</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Margraviate of Ivrea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=952&amp;focus=march-of-ivrea" aria-label="March of Ivrea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4867 574 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where March of Ivrea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5187 830L5218 839"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 839h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5187 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5187 830h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ivrea. <a href="/atlas?year=952&amp;focus=march-of-ivrea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

